			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2130223">
									

<p>+1</p>
<p>I have a strange, strange feeling that these aren't <em><strong>really</strong></em> anomalous. Hear me out. Yes, they reproduce in a way similar to an adorable &amp; fuzzy xenomorph&#8230;but that seems to be natural for them. At least, that's how I see it. They're strange, yes, but there are *far* stranger things in the animal kingdom. And that's part of why I'm +1ing this. It reminds me a little of the alien we have. A completely non-anomalous life-form that is really only being kept by the Foundation because while it's completely natural&#8230;it's just weird.</p>
<p>Though, while I might've missed it, do they have to use humans to reproduce? Or can they use other animals?</p>

